{
  "dom_id": "step-q128060",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Find the value of $(-\\frac{3}{8})÷\\frac{1}{6}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a negative number by a positive number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{8}÷\\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{3\\times 6}{8\\times 1}=\\frac{18}{8}=\\frac{9}{4},\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{3}{8})÷\\frac{1}{6}=-\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$",
